{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.md","line":419,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex#def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Curvature#def:dc-ch4-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-9]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","label":"def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form","line":977,"source":"\\begin{definition}[the index form $I_a$]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair, def:dc-ch4-2-1, def:dc-ch1-2-9}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.10}\n  For a geodesic $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$ and a vector field $V$ along $\\gamma$ with covariant\n  derivative $V'=\\frac{DV}{dt}$, the \\emph{index form} is\n  $$\n  I_a(V,V)=\\int_0^a\\{\\langle V',V'\\rangle-\\langle R(\\gamma',V)\\gamma',V\\rangle\\}\\,dt,\n  $$\n  with $R$ the curvature tensor and $\\gamma'$ the geodesic velocity. For a\n  proper variation, \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6} gives\n  $I_a(V,V)=\\frac{1}{2}E''(0)$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[the index form <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I_a$\">$I_a$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368392d322d31302d696e6465782d666f726d\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23def%3Adc-ch9-2-covariant-pair\">↗ def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh04_Curvature%23def%3Adc-ch4-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch4-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Adc-ch1-2-9\">↗ def:dc-ch1-2-9</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch9:2.10</span></span>For a geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$</span> and a vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span> along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> with covariant derivative <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V&#x27;=\\frac{DV}{dt}$\">$V&#x27;=\\frac{DV}{dt}$</span>, the <em>index form</em> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  I_a(V,V)=\\int _0^a\\{ \\langle V&#x27;,V&#x27;\\rangle -\\langle R(\\gamma &#x27;,V)\\gamma &#x27;,V\\rangle \\} \\, dt,  \\]\">\\[  I_a(V,V)=\\int _0^a\\{ \\langle V&#x27;,V&#x27;\\rangle -\\langle R(\\gamma &#x27;,V)\\gamma &#x27;,V\\rangle \\} \\, dt,  \\]</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R$\">$R$</span> the curvature tensor and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma &#x27;$\">$\\gamma &#x27;$</span> the geodesic velocity. For a proper variation, <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-10-formula6\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d31302d666f726d756c6136\">section 1</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I_a(V,V)=\\frac{1}{2}E&#x27;&#x27;(0)$\">$I_a(V,V)=\\frac{1}{2}E&#x27;&#x27;(0)$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-10-differentiation","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair","label":"def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Curvature#def:dc-ch4-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch4-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch4-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-9","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-9","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-9"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-3-1-index-form-scaled","title":"lem:dc-ch9-3-1-index-form-scaled","label":"lem:dc-ch9-3-1-index-form-scaled"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-3-1-index-sum-neg","title":"lem:dc-ch9-3-1-index-sum-neg","label":"lem:dc-ch9-3-1-index-sum-neg"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form","tex":"\\begin{definition}[the index form $I_a$]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch9-2-10-index-form}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair, def:dc-ch4-2-1, def:dc-ch1-2-9}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.10}\n  For a geodesic $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$ and a vector field $V$ along $\\gamma$ with covariant\n  derivative $V'=\\frac{DV}{dt}$, the \\emph{index form} is\n  $$\n  I_a(V,V)=\\int_0^a\\{\\langle V',V'\\rangle-\\langle R(\\gamma',V)\\gamma',V\\rangle\\}\\,dt,\n  $$\n  with $R$ the curvature tensor and $\\gamma'$ the geodesic velocity. For a\n  proper variation, \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-10-formula6} gives\n  $I_a(V,V)=\\frac{1}{2}E''(0)$.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-covariant-pair","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Curvature#def:dc-ch4-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch4-2-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-9","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-9","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}